# Frontend Rebuild Walkthrough

As requested, I have completely erased and recreated the three core pages to match the design images exactly.

## 1. Dashboard (The Command Center) - [app/page.tsx](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/app/page.tsx)
-   **Exact Match Sidebar**: Dark theme (`#111`), Red accents (`#E50914`), User profile at top, Issues count at bottom.
-   **White Theme Main Area**: Clean white background (`#FAFAFA`) with rounded cards (`rounded-[2rem]`).
    -   **Time Chart**: Uses `recharts` to render the blue/purple area chart with the specific "Time spent" tooltip.
    -   **Calendar**: Custom `react-calendar` implementation with the specific Red Box highlight for the active day.
    -   **Profile Card**: Matches the yellow "M" avatar and stats layout (Rank, Avg Hour, Enrolled).
    -   **Course & Homework**: Styled exactly as the bento grid in the image.

## 2. Learning Environment - [app/blackboard/page.tsx](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/app/blackboard/page.tsx)
-   **Dark Immersion**: Full screen dark background (`#121214`).
-   **Tools**: Floating bottom toolbar with requested icons (Hand, Pen, Eraser).
-   **AI Integration**: **Floating AI Widget** in the top-right. It starts as a small "Brain Orb" and expands into the chat interface, keeping the canvas clear as per your feedback.
-   **Infinite Canvas**: Re-implemented [BlackboardCanvas.tsx](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/components/BlackboardCanvas.tsx) for smooth zooming and panning.

## 3. Code Editor - [app/editor/page.tsx](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/STEM/frontend/app/editor/page.tsx)
-   **Split View Design**:
    -   **Left**: File Explorer (Minimal).
    -   **Center**: Monaco Editor in Light Theme (matching Image 2's white central area).
    -   **Right**: Console/Terminal in Dark Theme.
-   **Header**: "Python Playground" with the red "RUN CODE" button.
-   **Execution**: Powered by client-side Pyodide.

## Verification
All files have been strictly recreated. The components directory now contains only the necessary, high-fidelity components used in this rebuild.
